{
 "plan": {
  "title": "District Health Overview",
  "subtitle": "Key health indicators across districts",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Households Surveyed",
    "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Households surveyed\") AS n FROM district_health_factsheet",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Literate Women (15-49)",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", AVG(\"Women age 15-49 years who are literate (%)\") AS literacy FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "literacy"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Fully Vaccinated Children",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", AVG(\"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\") AS vaccination FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "vaccination"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Stunted Children Under 5",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", AVG(\"Children under 5 years who are stunted (%)\") AS stunting FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 ASC LIMIT 15",
    "x": "District",
    "y": [
     "stunting"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Sanitation Access",
    "sql": "SELECT \"District\", AVG(\"Households with improved sanitation facility (%)\") AS sanitation FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10"
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Survey Round Trends",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Survey Round\", AVG(\"Children age 12-23 months fully vaccinated (%)\") AS avg_vaccination FROM district_health_factsheet GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "Survey Round",
    "y": [
     "avg_vaccination"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "This dashboard provides a snapshot of key health indicators across districts. The 'Total Households Surveyed' KPI gives an overview of the data coverage. Bar charts illustrate the average literacy rates among women aged 15-49 and the percentage of children fully vaccinated, allowing for comparisons between districts. The 'Stunted Children Under 5' bar chart highlights areas needing focused intervention. A table shows sanitation access, and a line chart tracks vaccination trends over survey rounds. Further investigation into districts with low literacy or high stunting rates is recommended, using the data to inform targeted programs and resource allocation. The overall health status, as reflected by {{p1}}, is a key indicator of community well-being."
 },
